WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:38.700
Good morning,
everyone. It's 6:00 a.m. on Day 3.

00:00:38.866 --> 00:00:42.333
Okay, so this is a really cute
little restroom over here.

00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:46.766
Plus, it’s actually really clean,
and then we just use the rainwater from here to rinse it off.

00:00:46.866 --> 00:00:48.200
So why start off by talking
about the bathroom? I don't

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:49.700
know—I just happened to stop
by to use the restroom XD

00:00:49.933 --> 00:00:53.266
That's good. Yesterday—well,
yesterday we closed at 3,850.

00:00:53.266 --> 00:00:56.066
It's just spending the night on the summit of a snow
-capped mountain.

00:00:56.133 --> 00:00:59.700
Let me take a look over here,
but there aren't many places where you can pitch a tent,

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.966
Since this whole area is covered in granite and gravel,
it’s actually more like a gravel slope.

00:01:02.966 --> 00:01:06.433
Yesterday, we jokingly said that this is the path
from Xuezhu to Cuichi—something like that.

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:07.800
But it's not very long—it's
quite short.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.300
So what we see in the distance right now—that
tiny peak—is actually Luo's Peak.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:15.500
That's the high point, then Thumb Peak and Victoria
Peak—that's where we're heading next.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.700
According to the guide,

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:22.400
this is the toughest mountain. Over here, you can see there’s a rope you can use to climb up like this,
using the same belaying method we used yesterday.

00:01:22.566 --> 00:01:23.666
Oh, you can see this
in the background.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.766
We went to Alexander's
Peak yesterday.

00:01:26.766 --> 00:01:31.300
I spent the night at the summit of Mount 3850. Actually,
I slept pretty well—though I wouldn't say it was great.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.866
I didn't take any specific sleeping pills or anything
like that; I just took Yiweineng and slept soundly,

00:01:34.866 --> 00:01:38.433
Then, fully geared up,
I put on this thickest POWAY thermal shirt

00:01:38.433 --> 00:01:47.233
I used the sleeping bag provided by AVIDER, but it was made of synthetic fiber. I felt that since I was wearing a full PartyAlpha suit—including foot covers,
gloves, and a hood—plus a down jacket,

00:01:47.233 --> 00:01:51.900
Due to objective factors related to the campsite itself,
it is slightly sloped.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.700
It's just a little bit slanted,
so it slides around a bit like this.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:02:01.000
So here’s a tip: if the campsite is on a slope, make sure to sleep with your head elevated. It’s basic common sense,
but it’s still good for everyone to know.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:05.433
Here’s a little tip: if one side is lower than the other,
at the point where it’s lower,

00:02:05.433 --> 00:02:10.100
Stuff in some clothes or gear you might not need,
and then fill it up.

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:14.433
Make it at least a little flatter,
and tuck a backpack under your feet.

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:17.733
It'll help just a little bit,

00:02:17.933 --> 00:02:21.133
OK. So this is the little
hut where we eat.

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:25.700
Before that, it was military high
-altitude training; in Taiwan, that training takes place on Hehuan Mountain.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:30.900
After all, I'm a special forces soldier too,
but I've never trained there—yeah, I'm a total loser.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:35.900
Well, this is a spot that just opened
this year for the public to visit.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:40.033
So they don't usually train there all the time anyway,
so this little hut is open like that.

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:45.633
It was actually pretty interesting, though. Yesterday, the tour guide said that for the military training here,
they can only bring 12 people at a time.

00:02:45.633 --> 00:02:49.566
Because I've always wondered why this building is so small—it's really tiny,
to the point where you can actually bump your head on it.

00:02:49.566 --> 00:02:55.733
It's great because the altitude is high enough, so the high
-altitude training is very, very rigorous.

00:03:01.166 --> 00:03:03.166
At breakfast,

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:07.766
everyone's legs were really sore. So sore,
so sore—it's driving me crazy!

00:03:07.766 --> 00:03:08.466
Do you get a sour taste

00:03:08.466 --> 00:03:08.900
in your mouth? No?

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:09.466
No way! (I'm being grilled,

00:03:09.666 --> 00:03:11.666
XDDD)

00:03:12.166 --> 00:03:13.233
Do your legs ever get sore? No,

00:03:13.233 --> 00:03:15.166
they don't. I don't
feel any soreness.

00:03:15.366 --> 00:03:17.466
Wow, this scene is so beautiful!

00:03:17.466 --> 00:03:18.100
I don't feel anything.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.666
This scene is so beautiful!
I want to take

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.333
a picture—but they're still asleep.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:25.133
The guy who wasn't feeling well said
he was feeling a little better.

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:27.933
"This is a ZPacks sleeping bag,
" (Yeah.) "I use this one, too."

00:03:27.933 --> 00:03:31.633
390 grams, but mine has a zipper—mine
has a zipper.

00:03:31.633 --> 00:03:38.133
(Mine has a zipper.) Oh~ Wow, that brings back memories. I was going to bring it up here,
but I was too lazy, so I didn't.

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:41.433
This is very light; since it has a zipper,
it's not a down comforter.

00:03:41.433 --> 00:03:45.000
Since down comforters don't have zippers, they've released
a version with a zipper—but it's only 4 grams heavier.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:48.900
So I’d recommend that you all buy ones with zippers.
Everyone was just asking me if my legs were sore.

00:03:49.233 --> 00:03:52.166
I watched them—I watched them and felt a pang of envy,
and suddenly I felt that pang of envy too.

00:03:52.166 --> 00:03:56.600
Yeah, hahaha, but I think it's okay—I
guess that's just how group tours are.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:59.233
You don't have to cook,
prepare, or clean up after yourself.

00:03:59.233 --> 00:04:02.733
We just open our mouths whenever food comes our way—ahhhhh~~ We'll just eat it,
that's all.

00:04:02.733 --> 00:04:10.233
So it's no big deal—I don't have to worry about three meals a day,
and I feel like all my time is just really chill anyway.

00:04:10.233 --> 00:04:14.733
So when you see this one,
this one, this one, and this one—they're not dicks.

00:04:14.733 --> 00:04:19.900
This one, this one—this one is Mount Mugo,
as seen by Alexadar.

00:04:20.533 --> 00:04:22.033
Like this on my butt (???? Okay,

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:27.200
I really am a pervert...)

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:29.900
Sure! (??) Heart
-shaped

00:04:32.633 --> 00:04:33.566
mirror~~~

