00:06:17.066 --> 00:06:18.066
There's a rest stop in the middle.

00:06:21.466 --> 00:06:22.566
We'll make our way up
slowly like this.

00:06:26.866 --> 00:06:30.633
But since it rained here,
it's, um, a little wet.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:37.100
But your center of gravity is leaning too far forward—it’s actually not too bad,
though; this is pretty long.

00:06:41.566 --> 00:06:43.266
This rope is so juicy to the touch!

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:53.800
The highest point—yeah.

00:06:57.733 --> 00:07:00.933
Take some O2 capsules.

00:07:03.033 --> 00:07:06.800
The second one is black
and a little wet.

00:07:09.133 --> 00:07:10.700
It's quite slippery upstairs.

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:11.300
Okay.

00:07:11.833 --> 00:07:13.066
He said it's steep up there. Oh,

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:22.400
it's really wet over here—it's wet,
it's wet.

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:30.766
Okay, so I think it should go like this: pull with one hand like this,
then switch to the other hand.

00:07:30.766 --> 00:07:32.000
