Sure. Take this

00:41:28.500 --> 00:41:29.200
RC as well.

00:41:29.300 --> 00:41:29.566
Here. Just

00:41:29.633 --> 00:41:30.400
eat it.

00:41:30.900 --> 00:41:33.633
Eat them all—there are only two,
so yeah, eat them.

00:41:33.633 --> 00:41:34.866
So, do you want to take
some electrolytes? Sure,

00:41:34.866 --> 00:41:37.233
sure—I’ll take whatever
the CP has.

00:41:37.233 --> 00:41:40.333
Come on, come on, come on—this pill box is awesome.
It's really great.

00:41:40.533 --> 00:41:44.000
Because you'll forget what that color looks
like—do you know what color it is?

00:41:44.000 --> 00:41:44.966
Add a tag.

00:41:44.966 --> 00:41:45.433
No.

00:41:45.433 --> 00:41:46.700
If I come, you won't forget it.

00:41:47.233 --> 00:41:49.800
That's right—that's
why Celine invited me.

00:41:51.600 --> 00:41:54.766
That personal pharmacist—I
ask him once every day,

00:41:54.766 --> 00:41:58.500
CP, what’s that O2 for? (Altitude sickness,
altitude sickness!)

00:41:58.500 --> 00:41:59.333
It's been four days since I asked,

00:41:59.333 --> 00:42:01.800
right? They're going to rest once they reach 2K,
so we should be able to head out then.

00:42:02.133 --> 00:42:04.000
It's 12 o'clock now,

00:42:06.933 --> 00:42:07.733
so I'll definitely be able to head out before 4.
I put my clothes on backwards!!

00:42:07.866 --> 00:42:10.066
You've put your shirt on back to front again.
(Why are you here again?)

00:42:10.400 --> 00:42:11.200
How many times? I've
caught him wearing

00:42:11.200 --> 00:42:12.733
his socks on the wrong feet twice.

00:42:12.733 --> 00:42:16.233
Putting socks on the wrong way (twice with socks,
then once with clothes)

00:42:16.366 --> 00:42:19.700
And let me tell you, I never wear them on
the wrong way—it’s just that you’re

00:42:19.700 --> 00:42:21.966
I’ve put my clothes on backwards three times, and the one thing they all have in common is that you were there.
(Holding hands~~)

00:42:22.233 --> 00:42:23.666
So is it your problem?

00:42:23.966 --> 00:42:25.033
It's not my problem.

00:42:25.033 --> 00:42:27.233
Once in Hong Kong, once in Taiwan,
and once in Malaysia (wearing the "Backwards Master PRO"!)

00:42:27.366 --> 00:42:29.700
The point is, she just said with great pride,
“This looks great.”

00:42:31.100 --> 00:42:31.766
This is our campsite. Then
there are four peaks,

00:42:31.766 --> 00:42:36.633
and then that little cabin, right?

00:42:47.433 --> 00:42:50.233
"You are successful climbers"—that

00:42:50.233 --> 00:42:52.600
really resonates emotionally.

00:42:53.500 --> 00:42:55.133
Yay, we're here.

00:42:55.533 --> 00:42:56.600
1:28 p.m.

00:42:59.300 --> 00:43:04.000
Okay, let's head out. It'll take a total of 5 hours and 30 minutes,
plus time for a meal.

00:43:07.166 --> 00:43:10.033
(＊＆＾％＄＃＄％＾ (Anyway,
everyone was having a great time, haha))

